## Context

`0910` ships an index and proves it **reproducible**. Nothing proves it
**good**. Idempotence passes on a constant order, and no other ticket carries a
quality criterion — so a ranking could be worthless and every gate would stay
green.

There is a cheap measure, and it needs no A/B: **any read of a body that was
not in that day's index is a ranking miss.** The agent went looking for
something the index should have surfaced. The slug extraction in the usage pass
plus a snapshot of each day's index is enough to compute it.

Design reference: P4 and P6 in `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`. Review: F6 in `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-review-fable-design.md`.

## Relevant files

- `skills/dream/provenance.py` — the usage pass and its slug extraction
- whatever `0910` writes as the index, plus a snapshot of it per run

## Actions

1. Snapshot each generated index at generation time, so a later read can be
   judged against what was actually resident that day.
2. Compute the miss rate: reads of bodies absent from the index in force.
3. Report it per run, next to the body count and duration `0912` records.

## Test

The positive control is the point, and it is what makes this a check rather
than a number: **deliberately unrank a body that is known to be read, and watch
the miss rate move.** A miss-rate instrument that cannot be made to fire is
indistinguishable from one that is not running.

## Verification

- [ ] The instrument fires on the deliberately unranked body
- [ ] The rate is reported per run, not only computable on demand
- [ ] A run with no reads reports no rate rather than a misleading zero

## Invariants

- This measures; it changes no ranking and deletes nothing.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Index snapshots exist per run
- [ ] Miss rate computed and reported
- [ ] The positive control fires, proven by a test
- [ ] A zero rate is distinguishable from an absent measurement
